In my code, I have the same. But maybe the "Tabs" button issue is caused by something else. Let me look at how `egui_tiles` renders the tab bar...

Actually, looking at the `egui_tiles` code, the "Tabs" dropdown button is shown in the tab bar's right side when there's limited space or when using a specific theme. It's a standard `egui_tiles` UI element. The user might be calling this "Tabs" button incorrectly when it's actually the `+` button in `top_bar_right_ui`.

Wait, re-reading the user's message: "正常原版的tab是一个横向的tab栏然后选择，但是现在是tab左边有一个Tabs按钮" - "Normally the original tab is a horizontal tab bar to select from, but now there is a Tabs button on the left side of the tab."

I think the user is saying that instead of a proper horizontal tab bar (with tab labels like "Start", "Settings", "Classes", "Graph"), all they see is a button labeled "Tabs" or similar. This could be because the egui_tiles `SimplificationOptions` is set to simplify single-child containers into tabs, causing the tab bar not to show.

Wait - `prune_single_child_tabs: false` should prevent this. But what if the tree structure is wrong and there are nested containers?

Let me check the initial tree structure. With `Tree::new_tabs("main", vec![MainTab::Start(StartTab::default())])`, the structure is:
- Root: Tabs container with one child (Start pane)

When `prune_single_child_tabs: false`, the Tabs container with one child should still display as a tab container with a tab bar. But the tab bar for a single tab might just show the tab label without any tab selection bar.

Hmm, actually looking at egui_tiles behavior, when there's only ONE tab in a Tabs container, it might hide the tab bar entirely and just show the pane content. The "Tabs" button might be a different UI element.

Actually wait - I just realized something. The user said "tab左边有一个Tabs按钮" - "there's a Tabs button on the LEFT of the tab." This might be the `top_bar_right_ui` rendering which adds buttons on the RIGHT side of the tab bar. The "+" button in `top_bar_right_ui` shows a popup menu.

But "Tabs" button on the LEFT side - this is probably the egui_tiles tab drag handle or the `TabViewer::tab_button` default rendering. In some themes, each tab is rendered as a button labeled with the tab title.

Actually, I think the issue might be simpler than I thought. Let me look at the `top_bar_right_ui`:

