```

The `+` button opens a popup menu for adding tabs. The user might be calling this popup menu button the "Tabs button".

But the user said the tab bar is on the LEFT side, not right. `top_bar_right_ui` adds content to the RIGHT side of the tab bar. So a "Tabs" button on the left would be part of the DEFAULT tab bar rendering, not from `top_bar_right_ui`.

Hmm, let me think about this differently. The `egui_tiles::Tabs::ui` method renders each tab as a button in the tab bar. These buttons show the tab title. If the titles are showing as empty or "Tabs", it might be a different issue.

Actually, I think the actual problem might be the `tab_outline_stroke` returning `TRANSPARENT` color which makes the tab selection invisible, or the `tab_bg_color` making tabs look wrong.

Or maybe the issue is that the `for_all_tab_types!(tab, NAME)` macro doesn't work with the `$body:ident` syntax when `NAME` is a `const` and not an `ident`?

Let me check: `for_all_tab_types!(tab, NAME)` expands to `match tab { MainTab::Start(_) => StartTab::NAME, ... }`. `StartTab::NAME` is `"Start"`. This should work.

